WEBVTT

c0001
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.120
Good afternoon, ladies and gentlemen.

c0002
00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:10.280
My name is Marshall Wahlke.

c0003
00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:15.000
I'm consultant to Spurtus Institute for Continuing Education.

c0004
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:21.840
I want to welcome each and every one of you to this special Lunch and Learn lecture.

c0005
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:27.600
Before I introduce our guest speaker, I'd like to remind everyone of some of our upcoming

c0006
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.280
programs.

c0007
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:34.200
Listen to Yiddish Language and Culture, an intensive four-day course, begins this coming

c0008
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.200
Monday.

c0009
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:41.320
The course will be taught by our ever-popular Professor Nathaniel Stanford.

c0010
00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:47.160
This coming Sunday, the Jewish Film Project will present the Academy Award-winning The

c0011
00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:54.240
Shop on Main Street at 1.30 p.m. at the Film Center of the Art Institute.

c0012
00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.639
This museum is currently offering two important exhibitions.

c0013
00:00:58.639 --> 00:01:06.919
Marianne's Truth Paintings, 1957 to 1975, displays the works of this provocative artist

c0014
00:01:06.919 --> 00:01:11.559
and Holocaust survivor who developed his own expressive style.

c0015
00:01:11.559 --> 00:01:18.959
Next Thursday, July 18th at 6 p.m., Richard Francis, Chief Curator of the Museum of Contemporary

c0016
00:01:18.959 --> 00:01:25.000
Art, will discuss Marianne in the context of the contemporary art world.

c0017
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:31.839
The exhibition, Precincts, Parties, and Platforms, Politics and Chicago Jews, is on display on

c0018
00:01:31.839 --> 00:01:34.199
this floor just outside the auditorium.

c0019
00:01:34.199 --> 00:01:39.199
If you didn't have time to see it before, make it your business to see it later.

c0020
00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:45.879
And next Tuesday evening, July 16th from 6.30 to 8.30, Dr. Faul, who will be delivering

c0021
00:01:45.879 --> 00:01:52.440
today's lecture, will present Maimonides as a mystic, offering a new perspective on

c0022
00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.599
the great Jewish philosopher.

c0023
00:01:54.599 --> 00:01:59.959
All of these programs and more are explained in detail in our calendar of events, which

c0024
00:01:59.959 --> 00:02:06.839
you can pick up right outside this room at the table or in the various display stands

c0025
00:02:06.839 --> 00:02:08.479
throughout the building.

c0026
00:02:08.479 --> 00:02:13.899
And now I'd like to tell you a little about the fascinating background of Dr. Jose Faul,

c0027
00:02:13.899 --> 00:02:17.500
who joins us today from Israel as our guest speaker.

c0028
00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:23.860
I noticed as people started coming in, most of you know him, and he knows most of you

c0029
00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:25.259
by name, which is remarkable.

c0030
00:02:25.259 --> 00:02:29.220
Of course, he's not a stranger to the Spurtus.

c0031
00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:32.179
Professor Faul is an ordained Sepharadi Rabbi.

c0032
00:02:32.179 --> 00:02:38.419
He received his B.A., M.A., and Ph.D. from the University of Barcelona in the Department

c0033
00:02:38.419 --> 00:02:40.339
of Semitic Philology.

c0034
00:02:40.339 --> 00:02:46.339
He has taught at the Jewish Theological Seminary, Columbia University, the Pontifical University

c0035
00:02:46.339 --> 00:02:55.300
of Salamanica, University of Haifa, the Sepharadi Heritage Foundation, and Spurtus College of

c0036
00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.500
Judaica.

c0037
00:02:56.500 --> 00:03:00.300
He's currently teaching at Bar-Ilan University in Israel.

c0038
00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:07.259
He has written five books and published over 60 articles, establishing himself as a specialist

c0039
00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:14.380
in a wide number of fields, including theology, philosophy, law, history, and linguistics.

c0040
00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:20.380
Today, Dr. Faul will speak on Jewish law in the postmodern world.

c0041
00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:27.660
Please join me in welcoming Dr. Faul.

c0042
00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:29.779
Thank you very much.

c0043
00:03:29.779 --> 00:03:40.619
Coming from Israel, I have to tell you, I feel I am at home here.

c0044
00:03:40.619 --> 00:03:48.020
It's great, super, to feel the warmth of the Spurtus family.

c0045
00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:51.539
We are a family.

c0046
00:03:51.539 --> 00:03:54.899
This is the spirit of Spurtus.

c0047
00:03:54.899 --> 00:04:01.580
And because I feel I am at home, I'm going to be less formal, all right?

c0048
00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:09.779
And I want to discuss something with you, a Jewish halakha.

c0049
00:04:09.779 --> 00:04:21.260
We Jews are what we are because we have a system of values that we call law.

c0050
00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:28.299
We have a misva, a misva, and we do it.

c0051
00:04:28.299 --> 00:04:35.980
And we strive to behave according to certain model.

c0052
00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:53.059
I believe that the model of Jewish halakha will be the model of the postmodern human.

c0053
00:04:53.059 --> 00:05:07.579
I believe postmodern humanity will have to strive to design some sort of a model that

c0054
00:05:07.579 --> 00:05:18.059
if you look carefully at that model, you will find a halakha.

c0055
00:05:18.059 --> 00:05:30.260
Before going into the specificity, the particulars of that model, let me point out two very interesting

c0056
00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:33.820
aspects.

c0057
00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:40.220
Number one, the meaning of the word halakha.

c0058
00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:46.420
halakha is a road, a path.

c0059
00:05:46.420 --> 00:06:00.540
Something that was a charter, and it is one of the ways in which you can walk, but there

c0060
00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:04.940
is nobody pushing you there.

c0061
00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:18.739
As it were, life's bifurcates, it opens up, and among the various avenues, there is a

c0062
00:06:18.739 --> 00:06:31.940
special road, and at your own, nobody is telling you what to do because nobody can tell you

c0063
00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:35.380
how to choose.

c0064
00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:41.500
You decide to go in a special halakha.

c0065
00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:44.660
halakha means halicha, going.

c0066
00:06:44.660 --> 00:06:48.660
You go.

c0067
00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:53.660
That is one aspect of halakha.

c0068
00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:59.859
Let's see the results of halakha.

c0069
00:06:59.859 --> 00:07:05.059
halakha is a miracle in history.

c0070
00:07:05.059 --> 00:07:15.619
No other people performed the miracle that we Jewish people performed.

c0071
00:07:15.619 --> 00:07:28.299
As a matter of fact, if you want to understand utopia, not in mythological terms, not in

c0072
00:07:28.299 --> 00:07:38.260
science fiction structures, but in a real human way, you have to think about halakha.

c0073
00:07:38.260 --> 00:07:39.260
How?

c0074
00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:51.820
For 2,000 years, we, the Jewish people, lived without a police force.

c0075
00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:56.739
There was no police in the Jewish ghetto.

c0076
00:07:56.739 --> 00:08:06.019
There was no police force in Warsaw, in Vilna, in Izmir, in Istanbul, in the first quarters

c0077
00:08:06.019 --> 00:08:11.579
where the Jews lived, telling us how to behave.

c0078
00:08:11.579 --> 00:08:24.739
The ideal of humanity is when people, men, women, children, all, they could get together,

c0079
00:08:24.739 --> 00:08:33.020
fight, disagree, without having to have recourse to violence.

c0080
00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:36.059
I am proud.

c0081
00:08:36.059 --> 00:08:48.580
I am very proud of belonging to a nation, to a people, that we were able to flourish

c0082
00:08:48.580 --> 00:08:55.820
together without a police force.

c0083
00:08:55.820 --> 00:09:04.900
And if some of our Gentile friends question the contribution of Judaism, I would use one

c0084
00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:09.020
word, halakha.

c0085
00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:12.260
But there's other aspects to halakha.

c0086
00:09:13.219 --> 00:09:20.419
halakha means a dynamic concept of humans.

c0087
00:09:20.419 --> 00:09:24.380
We are not what we are.

c0088
00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:28.739
We are what we choose to be.

c0089
00:09:28.739 --> 00:09:34.859
And choosing, it means a dynamic motion.

c0090
00:09:34.859 --> 00:09:37.299
You have to walk.

c0091
00:09:37.299 --> 00:09:44.739
You have to pursue a specific itinerary.

c0092
00:09:44.739 --> 00:09:56.059
halakha means that you have a point of departure and you have an aim.

c0093
00:09:56.059 --> 00:10:04.099
You want to reach a destination.

c0094
00:10:04.340 --> 00:10:07.659
People live.

c0095
00:10:07.659 --> 00:10:10.979
Jews walk.

c0096
00:10:10.979 --> 00:10:16.979
Jews are in a constant motion.

c0097
00:10:16.979 --> 00:10:21.979
halakha means I am not passive.

c0098
00:10:21.979 --> 00:10:25.260
I am not static.

c0099
00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:33.979
I am a person with an aim.

c0100
00:10:33.979 --> 00:10:52.140
But in modern times, specifically with the Enlightenment, modernity made it a taboo.

c0101
00:10:52.140 --> 00:11:01.179
halakha became something primitive.

c0102
00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:10.380
Something that only unintelligent, unenlightened people follow.

c0103
00:11:10.380 --> 00:11:22.900
Rousseau, the father of modernity, the great French philosopher that in a way is the father

c0104
00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:38.700
of the French Revolution, of modern constitutions, of liberty, equality, fraternity, defines

c0105
00:11:38.700 --> 00:11:47.739
modern society in terms that exclude halakha.

c0106
00:11:47.739 --> 00:11:50.739
Why?

c0107
00:11:50.739 --> 00:12:03.140
For Rousseau, for the French intellectuals, everything, the future, whatever you want

c0108
00:12:03.140 --> 00:12:10.580
to, it must be now, right here.

c0109
00:12:10.619 --> 00:12:23.940
To be modern means specifically to be a non-halachist, not to have a past, and there is no other

c0110
00:12:23.940 --> 00:12:27.539
goal what you have to reach.

c0111
00:12:27.539 --> 00:12:37.619
The present, incorporated in the state, is everything we want.

c0112
00:12:37.659 --> 00:12:46.659
Perfection, holiness, purity, whatever you want, you don't have it in the past.

c0113
00:12:46.659 --> 00:12:56.659
There will be no Messiah, because if there is a Messiah, it's here, now.

c0114
00:12:56.659 --> 00:13:03.659
Perfection is in the state.

c0115
00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:16.700
The state is the ultimate rod, the cannon by which you measure everything.

c0116
00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:28.700
And therefore, if you wanted to be modern, you have to cut the umbilical cord with the

c0117
00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:30.700
past.

c0118
00:13:30.739 --> 00:13:40.739
You have to renounce to a Messiah, because everything is in the state.

c0119
00:13:40.739 --> 00:13:49.739
Moreover, even you as an individual, you are not you.

c0120
00:13:49.780 --> 00:13:59.780
If you want to be modern, you are what society says you are.

c0121
00:13:59.780 --> 00:14:04.780
What the state says you are.

c0122
00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:13.780
There is a God, but God works for the state.

c0123
00:14:13.820 --> 00:14:26.820
You could have a religion, but the religion has to be subordinated to the state.

c0124
00:14:26.820 --> 00:14:32.820
There is no real separation between church and state.

c0125
00:14:32.820 --> 00:14:41.820
The state issues licenses to churches, temples, etc.

c0126
00:14:41.859 --> 00:14:46.859
And in a way, and we know it in France, it's true.

c0127
00:14:46.859 --> 00:14:51.859
Even the Rabbi's salary is paid by the state.

c0128
00:14:51.859 --> 00:15:06.859
So, to be modern, if you're intelligent, you have to divest yourself from halakha.

c0129
00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:16.900
Now, let us talk about early days.

c0130
00:15:16.900 --> 00:15:23.900
The very beginning of humanity.

c0131
00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:30.940
The scripture tells us about two men.

c0132
00:15:30.940 --> 00:15:39.940
One by the name of Hebel, and the other by the name of Cain.

c0133
00:15:39.940 --> 00:15:52.940
We know that Hebel was a shepherd, and Cain was Ish Adama, a man of the land.

c0134
00:15:52.979 --> 00:16:02.979
We know also that our forefathers were shepherds.

c0135
00:16:02.979 --> 00:16:13.979
Abraham, Jacob, King David, they were shepherds.

c0136
00:16:14.020 --> 00:16:20.020
And when Joseph's brethren were coming to Egypt,

c0137
00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:28.020
Joseph tells to his brothers, I will introduce you to Pharaoh,

c0138
00:16:28.020 --> 00:16:36.020
and tell him what your profession is.

c0139
00:16:36.059 --> 00:16:45.059
And they introduced themselves as raim anahnu, we are shepherds.

c0140
00:16:45.059 --> 00:16:57.059
And the scripture tells us that shepherds for Egypt were an abomination.

c0141
00:16:57.059 --> 00:17:02.059
What does it mean to be a shepherd?

c0142
00:17:02.099 --> 00:17:12.099
Why was it so important to identify yourself as a shepherd?

c0143
00:17:12.099 --> 00:17:24.099
I believe that there are two ways in which society could organize itself.

c0144
00:17:24.099 --> 00:17:30.099
It could organize itself in terms of space.

c0145
00:17:30.140 --> 00:17:41.140
This is our land, geography, a border.

c0146
00:17:41.140 --> 00:17:52.140
And those who are comprised within this space will be guaranteed certain rights,

c0147
00:17:52.140 --> 00:17:56.140
will have certain duties.

c0148
00:17:56.180 --> 00:18:01.180
And no matter how you call this organization,

c0149
00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:08.180
there is always a big brother looking at you,

c0150
00:18:08.180 --> 00:18:18.180
and saying, you are here, and you must behave accordingly.

c0151
00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:25.180
And if you leave out, well, we have nothing to do with you.

c0152
00:18:25.219 --> 00:18:31.219
You are what you are by virtue of space.

c0153
00:18:31.219 --> 00:18:34.219
That is one way.

c0154
00:18:34.219 --> 00:18:41.219
That was the way Cain conceived society.

c0155
00:18:41.219 --> 00:18:48.219
He was ish adama, a man of the land.

c0156
00:18:48.260 --> 00:18:52.260
As a matter of fact, the scripture says,

c0157
00:18:52.260 --> 00:18:58.260
that as soon as Cain began to wander, wandering around,

c0158
00:18:58.260 --> 00:19:04.260
that even here he built a city.

c0159
00:19:04.260 --> 00:19:13.260
Man is determined, defined, confined by space.

c0160
00:19:13.260 --> 00:19:16.260
Very good.

c0161
00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:24.300
When you are a shepherd, you are in the desert.

c0162
00:19:24.300 --> 00:19:29.300
In Hebrew, in the Hebrew of the scripture,

c0163
00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:36.300
a desert is not a desolated place.

c0164
00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:42.300
It is a place where there is pasture for the sheep,

c0165
00:19:42.339 --> 00:19:50.339
and is outside any government jurisdiction.

c0166
00:19:50.339 --> 00:19:55.339
And because there is no government,

c0167
00:19:55.339 --> 00:20:01.339
you could pasture any way you want to.

c0168
00:20:01.339 --> 00:20:05.339
But there is a drawback.

c0169
00:20:05.380 --> 00:20:16.380
What happens if you are pasturing at your favorite spot,

c0170
00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:23.380
and all of a sudden, as with our forefather Jacob,

c0171
00:20:23.380 --> 00:20:26.380
there are other shepherds.

c0172
00:20:26.380 --> 00:20:30.380
There is no police.

c0173
00:20:30.420 --> 00:20:36.420
How are you going to deal with the situation?

c0174
00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:40.420
You are going to kill them?

c0175
00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:44.420
You are going to run away?

c0176
00:20:44.420 --> 00:20:49.420
To be a shepherd in the biblical tradition

c0177
00:20:49.420 --> 00:20:54.420
means that you are willing to negotiate.

c0178
00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:58.420
Horizontally.

c0179
00:20:58.459 --> 00:21:02.459
Let's try to find a solution.

c0180
00:21:02.459 --> 00:21:06.459
Maybe you go to shepherd, deal with the sheep

c0181
00:21:06.459 --> 00:21:10.459
on the east side, I on the west side.

c0182
00:21:10.459 --> 00:21:14.459
Maybe you in the early morning, I in the late morning.

c0183
00:21:14.459 --> 00:21:19.459
If you are a shepherd,

c0184
00:21:19.459 --> 00:21:26.459
you must find common grounds

c0185
00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:30.500
and negotiate.

c0186
00:21:30.500 --> 00:21:38.500
And out of this mode of operating,

c0187
00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:45.500
a new idea develops into the world.

c0188
00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:51.500
A covenant, an alliance,

c0189
00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:55.540
not only among ourselves,

c0190
00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:59.540
but as our forefathers did

c0191
00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:03.540
at the foot of Mount Sinai,

c0192
00:22:03.540 --> 00:22:07.540
a covenant with God.

c0193
00:22:07.540 --> 00:22:13.540
And let's try to make, find a way

c0194
00:22:13.540 --> 00:22:19.540
in which we could deal with ourselves

c0195
00:22:19.579 --> 00:22:23.579
and God and us could have

c0196
00:22:23.579 --> 00:22:27.579
a relationship.

c0197
00:22:27.579 --> 00:22:31.579
In Hebrew, there is a word, Berit.

c0198
00:22:31.579 --> 00:22:35.579
Berit is a covenant,

c0199
00:22:35.579 --> 00:22:39.579
is an alliance, is a bilateral contract

c0200
00:22:39.579 --> 00:22:43.579
between us the people of Israel

c0201
00:22:43.579 --> 00:22:47.579
and God.

c0202
00:22:47.619 --> 00:22:51.619
And therefore, here we have

c0203
00:22:51.619 --> 00:22:55.619
something new.

c0204
00:22:55.619 --> 00:22:59.619
A system of values

c0205
00:22:59.619 --> 00:23:03.619
that we call Kiroshim, holy, sacred

c0206
00:23:03.619 --> 00:23:07.619
because we promise we are not going to violate them

c0207
00:23:07.619 --> 00:23:11.619
and even when we violate

c0208
00:23:11.619 --> 00:23:15.619
this covenant, we say, I'm sorry, I will try not to do it again.

c0209
00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:19.660
And we have a covenant

c0210
00:23:19.660 --> 00:23:23.660
and this will allow us

c0211
00:23:23.660 --> 00:23:27.660
not only to survive

c0212
00:23:27.660 --> 00:23:31.660
but to be a paradigm to the world. Why?

c0213
00:23:31.660 --> 00:23:35.660
Because our system of values

c0214
00:23:35.660 --> 00:23:39.660
does not depend on space.

c0215
00:23:39.660 --> 00:23:43.660
On the values of a nomad.

c0216
00:23:43.699 --> 00:23:47.699
You could be anywhere in the world

c0217
00:23:47.699 --> 00:23:51.699
and you are bound by the same

c0218
00:23:51.699 --> 00:23:55.699
Tora, by the same misva,

c0219
00:23:55.699 --> 00:23:59.699
by the same ideals.

c0220
00:23:59.699 --> 00:24:03.699
You could be a nomad.

c0221
00:24:03.699 --> 00:24:07.699
You don't depend on space.

c0222
00:24:07.699 --> 00:24:11.699
Instead of space,

c0223
00:24:11.739 --> 00:24:15.739
we Jews

c0224
00:24:15.739 --> 00:24:19.739
inhabit time.

c0225
00:24:19.739 --> 00:24:23.739
To be a Jew means

c0226
00:24:23.739 --> 00:24:27.739
to be a citizen of a dimension

c0227
00:24:27.739 --> 00:24:31.739
called time. And why?

c0228
00:24:31.739 --> 00:24:35.739
Because we have a past.

c0229
00:24:35.739 --> 00:24:39.739
Because we have a history.

c0230
00:24:39.780 --> 00:24:43.780
Because we have tradition.

c0231
00:24:43.780 --> 00:24:47.780
And to have a past

c0232
00:24:47.780 --> 00:24:51.780
it means that you have a future.

c0233
00:24:51.780 --> 00:24:55.780
